title: Federated wiki followed by forking for a decade before skg, and what its users met says what to build and what to leave alone.
pid: 0d49b634-b190-48b0-8656-c99f824d19c0
body: |2-
  Ward Cunningham's federated wiki (from 2011, fed.wiki.org): each
  person's pages live on their own site; one edits another's page by
  forking the whole page to one's own site, and every page carries a
  journal of the actions that made it, a fork among them, with its date
  and the site it came from. Read whole on 2026-11-15, by 'curl':
  fed.wiki.org's pages "Journal", "Neighborhood" and "Review Changes";
  'emitTwins' in 'lib/refresh.js' of github.com/fedwiki/wiki-client;
  Caulfield's "Federated Wiki, Slow Cooperation, and a Kindle Parable"
  (hapgood.us, 2015-01-08) and the post it answers, Frances Bell's
  "Reflection on #fedwiki: Two Tales of Two Forks" (2015-01-05). Known
  only from a search engine's summary: that the project stalled, and why.
contains:
